---
import StaticPage from '../layouts/StaticPage.astro';
import { SITE_NAME } from '../consts';
---

<StaticPage
  title="Editorial Policy"
  description={`The editorial standards and practices of ${SITE_NAME}.`}
  canonicalPath="/editorial-policy/"
  updated="September 2026"
>
  <p>
    {SITE_NAME} is committed to accuracy, fairness, and transparency in everything
    we publish. This policy outlines the standards that guide our reporting.
  </p>

  <h2>Accuracy and verification</h2>
  <p>
    We strive to verify facts before publication using primary sources, official
    records, and on-the-record contacts. When information is developing, we label
    it clearly and update stories as confirmed details emerge.
  </p>

  <h2>Sourcing</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Every story attributes its originating source by name and, where applicable, link.</li>
    <li>We prefer on-the-record sources and identify them whenever possible.</li>
    <li>Anonymous sources are used only when information cannot be obtained otherwise and the reason is explained to readers.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Independence</h2>
  <p>
    Editorial content is produced independently of advertising, sponsorship, or
    commercial relationships. Sponsors have no influence over story selection,
    framing, or conclusions.
  </p>

  <h2>Balance and fairness</h2>
  <p>
    On contested matters of public interest, we seek relevant perspectives and give
    subjects of reporting a meaningful opportunity to respond.
  </p>

  <h2>Updates and transparency</h2>
  <p>
    Material updates to a story are noted with a revised timestamp and, where
    appropriate, a correction notice. See our{' '}
    <a href="/corrections-policy/">Corrections Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Sponsored and generated content</h2>
  <p>
    Any sponsored or partnered content is clearly labeled and kept visually distinct
    from editorial reporting. Automated content, when introduced, will be labeled
    and subject to human editorial review before publication.
  </p>
</StaticPage>
